{"id": "EUVD-2026-76351", "enisaUuid": "8f3965b8-52b6-3df0-b154-ba13a4b7cbcb", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommufd: Fix UAF in selftest IOPF reporting\n\nIOMMUFD selftest TRIGGER_IOPF borrows an attach handle from\ngroup->pasid_array without synchronizing against PASID detach,\nthen a concurrent iommu_report_device_fault() can dereference\nthat borrowed handle's domain pointer after the detach erases\nthe handle and frees the backing struct iommufd_attach_handle.\nTRIGGER_IOPF then dereferences the freed handle, causing a UAF.\n\nFix by adding a iopf_rwsem in mock_dev to follow the expected design\nof a real driver. Hold its read side across the whole\niommu_report_device_fault() call, and its write side around every\npath that attaches, detaches, or replaces a device domain.\nThis can block new reports and drains in-flight reports before an old\nattach handle or the IOPF fault parameter can be removed.\nAlso take the write side while registering a mock device, since\nit can invoke the mock driver's default-domain attach callback.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:54", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd2e7ac94d6d813548b021473c3dddc30c8c07d1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cab2895729516799384d48560e6fca105fb3f927", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e27e90bde68b2ab92e63ed19caad1ef57188bea0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c07df7cdfcf52f1ff276c588612aabc6c6b8399"], "aliases": ["GHSA-52p7-c9pg-r5j6", "CVE-2026-89445"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0381db9c-f3ea-3b22-b754-18c7eb3a7ac4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddee19971081b42615d62f4fdada21274708ed4d <fd2e7ac94d6d813548b021473c3dddc30c8c07d1"}, {"id": "2718960c-ac0b-3abd-992b-0d12f71d1d0c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddee19971081b42615d62f4fdada21274708ed4d <cab2895729516799384d48560e6fca105fb3f927"}, {"id": "280d08d3-35a6-31fe-93e3-facb386fd6af", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "61dd217b-db38-3d3c-a5a5-c84d73d70343", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.11"}, {"id": "71a970d6-2f58-311e-b287-065ae06248bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddee19971081b42615d62f4fdada21274708ed4d <8c07df7cdfcf52f1ff276c588612aabc6c6b8399"}, {"id": "73599024-5bd5-3815-9d65-c90e5a7b6c3f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "793d2e31-70e6-3d0a-8f78-78c39dba2a91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddee19971081b42615d62f4fdada21274708ed4d <e27e90bde68b2ab92e63ed19caad1ef57188bea0"}, {"id": "89805007-095c-3ea6-9d1a-1c2b6a1ed347", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "adfb0bad-8b77-3c3f-897d-01ea3b216e50", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "bebc96af-30b3-3273-a6cf-b31bbf0920d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ddcde4b6-8728-3425-ac23-21410e096501", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}